  "algorithm": [
    "Parse header, slot1 DICT and each texture directly in a separate Python reader. Resolve every relative pointer from its own field as signed32; read TXOB +0x38 as the pointer to the 32-byte image descriptor. Compare counts, names, dimensions, format, bpp, mip count, payload offset and size with the C API.",
    "For raw samples use a fixed literal 8x8 Morton-position matrix. Source pixel index = ((y//8)*(stored_width//8)+x//8)*64+matrix[y%8][x%8]. RGBA8 reverses the four source bytes. RGBA4 reads a little-endian word and expands its high-to-low nibbles by17. RGB565 expands r5/g6/b5 by bit replication, with alpha255.",
    "For ETC1/ETC1A4 decode each stored color block with the pinned unmodified AOSP reference, reversing its8 bytes to the standard MSB-first stream. Independently assemble source block=(tile*4)+[[0,1],[2,3]][(y%8)//4][(x%8)//4]. The RGB pixel index within that block is ((y%4)*4+x%4). Alpha nibble index is4*(x%4)+y%4 in the8-byte prefix, low nibble first, multiplied by17. ETC1 uses alpha255.",
    "Compare complete tightly packed top-down RGBA byte arrays, not just hashes. Record SHA256 after equality. Verify source buffers are unchanged after closing all borrowed CGFX indexes."
  ],
  "commands": [
    "tools/native-build/bin/cc -std=c11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic -shared -fPIC native/assets/etc1.c native/assets/texture.c native/assets/cgfx.c -o outputs/native-cgfx/libpx_cgfx.so",
    "AOSP reference setup and hashes: native/reproduction/texture-formats/reference-comparison.json; local shared library outputs/native-textures/reference/libaosp_etc1.so.",
